{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "2027 CAN bootloader allocation for eligible custom boards; explicit user exclusions are retained as reserved IDs.",
  "addressing": {
    "frame_format": "standard_11_bit",
    "host_can_id": "0x000",
    "node_id_min": 1,
    "node_id_max": 40,
    "node_rx_formula": "node_id",
    "node_tx_formula": "node_id + 0x28",
    "node_rx_can_id_range": [
      "0x001",
      "0x028"
    ],
    "node_tx_can_id_range": [
      "0x029",
      "0x050"
    ],
    "direction": "RX and TX are relative to the board: host sends to rx_can_id, board responds on tx_can_id."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Node IDs are stable board identities, not application message IDs. Do not renumber assigned boards when removing another board.",
    "can_buses lists physical attachment from the DBCs, not enabled bootloader transports. No routing, gateway or bootloader implementation is configured by this file.",
    "SMBs are battery monitoring boards without CAN and are intentionally excluded.",
    "External/bootloader host and COTS devices are not board allocations.",
    "Bottom-shell lighting is integrated on DEI; it is not a separate programmable board.",
    "ElconInterface is intentionally excluded from this bootloader allocation; its DBC node and application traffic remain.",
    "MIKA and TelemetryLeader are one physical node, named MIKA in the DBCs; both names are excluded from this bootloader allocation.",
    "Removed node IDs 5, 9, 11 and 12 remain reserved; all remaining board node/RX/TX IDs are unchanged."
  ],
  "reserved_node_ids": [
    5,
    9,
    11,
